{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1559476-rosmerta-the-great-provider-goddess-of-abundance-nemetondevos","id":1559476,"title":"Rosmerta, The Great Provider, Goddess of Abundance - Nemetondevos","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-04-17T02:02:06-07:00","id":1559476,"title":"Rosmerta, The Great Provider, Goddess of Abundance - Nemetondevos","content":"I was thinking about how it is hard to separate the Gaulish gods from Roman influence, and decided to write up Rosmerta, the Gaulish consort goddess to Mercury. Please let me know any comments or suggestions. Thanks!<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"color:#3465a4\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Rosmerta does not remember the Battle of Alesia, or the time before it. Perhaps that was before her Apotheosis. Or perhaps she was the companion of another god; the mysterious Lugos, or some other. It doesn\u2019t matter. Rosmerta knows only that the goddess that she can remember being came into existence after Alesia, after the fall of most of the other Nemetondevos. And so she chose a different path, the path of accommodation with the conquerors of Gaul. She became the help-meet \u2013 some would say consort \u2013 of Mercury in Gaul, easing his way into the hearts and minds of the Gaulish people.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#3465a4\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">She provided, and he traded. She gave, and he exchanged. The two of them worked well together \u2013 or so she thought. If her people were to survive, they would need to adapt to Roman ways, Roman thinking; they would need an intercessor \u2013 and Rosmerta believed she could be that link. She could help bridge the connections between the conqueror and the conquered. The Gauls loved her, and because of that, the combined worship of Mercury and Rosmerta spread.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#3465a4\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">But over time, Rosmerta found herself changing, accommodating Mercury more and more, becoming more what he needed her to be, and less independent. Eventually, she realized her mistake. She had become everything Mercury needed her to be until Mercury didn\u2019t need her anymore; he could <i>be</i> her. But by then it was too late, and Mercury\u2019s harpe slit her godly throat, spilling her golden ichor upon her sacred nemeton.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#3465a4\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Rosmerta realized in her dying moments that Mercury never loved her, never appreciated her. She were just a tool to him, a means to allow him to gain acceptance among the Gauls, and enact his will among the people. Once his worship had spread throughout the land, and he had collected the Mantles of so many of his predecessors, what value did she have?</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#3465a4\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The absorption of Rosmerta\u2019s identity was so complete, to the point where she was now depicted as a female Mercury, cadeceus in her hands and wings upon her head.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#3465a4\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Now Rosmerta has been reborn into the World. She feels the pull to Mercury \u2013 who is Rosmerta without Mercury? \u2013 but remembers the sting of his betrayal. Can she forge a path that is all her own?</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#3465a4\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Callings: Lover, Guardian, Healer</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#3465a4\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Purviews: Fertility, Fortune, Health, Prosperity</span></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28946-pryderi","name":"Pryderi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}